Eric W. Sink (e-sink@uiuc.edu) wrote:
: I can't find enough rings!!  :-(  I have slain everything in sight on
: every level I could find.  I completed the quest, killed everyone in
: Fort Ludios, and everyone in dungeon levels 1-24.  Through all this I
: have been unable to find a ring of levitation to get across the water
: on the medusa level and the moat in Fort Ludios.  I can't find water
: walking boots either.  I've seen hundreds of pairs of low boots and
: high boots (all those soldiers I creamed).  The exact list of rings I
: have discovered:

Have you found a wand of polymorph.  You hundreds of pairs of boots
should yield at one water walking boots.

How about a wand of cold?  Usually something near Fort Ludios carries
one.  You can use that to freeze the moat.  The same goes for medusa
level.

: Am I missing something ?  I still have yet to receive a wish, though
: someone said I should possibly have found a magic lamp in the Gnome
: town.  I did find several lamps, and rubbed them all (Nothing happens),
: but I didn't bless any of them.  Is it worth a trip back to the town
: to try that?

Did you try to rub them more than once?  It usually takes a few tries to
get the first puff of smoke.  When I do, its blessing time.

: Is it common to simply get stuck because you've run out of new things
: to find and can't get across water?

Its pretty tough.  There are several ways to get across the castle moat,
one of which is by playing an instrument.  Also since you have polymorph
control, you might be able to level teleport below the Medusa level and
go up the stairs (with eyes closed of course).

